  "reading": "The mechanism is real and too small. With an exact kernel, no calibration error, no sky and no crowding, the ratio falls monotonically from 0.99921 at point-like to 0.99338 at the largest size -- a decline of 0.00407. So segment photometry on PSF-matched frames does produce a size-dependent ratio, by construction and with nothing else to blame. But the catalogue shows 0.144, roughly 35 times larger. This accounts for about 3% of the observed bias and cannot be the whole of it.",
